<https://fhir-ig.digitalhealth.gov.ng/Basic/NgCoreResponder> a fhir:Basic ;
  fhir:nodeRole fhir:treeRoot ;
  fhir:Resource.id [ fhir:value "NgCoreResponder"] ;
  fhir:DomainResource.text [
     fhir:Narrative.status [ fhir:value "generated" ] ;
     fhir:Narrative.div "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><p class=\"res-header-id\"><b>Generated Narrative: ActorDefinition NgCoreResponder</b></p><a name=\"NgCoreResponder\"> </a><a name=\"hcNgCoreResponder\"> </a><table class=\"grid\"><tr><td><b>Actor: NgCoreResponder </b></td><td>Nigeria Core Responder</td><td>Type: system </td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"3\"><div><h3>Role</h3>\n<p>The <strong>Nigeria Core Responder</strong> is an authorised FHIR-enabled service that\nreceives and processes requests.</p>\n<p>Examples include FHIR servers, EMR/EHR back ends, HIEs, registries,\nlaboratory, pharmacy and imaging services, program platforms, gateways,\nterminology services, and sandbox services.</p>\n<h3>Responsibilities</h3>\n<p>A Responder may:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>receive REST requests, operations, Bundles, documents, or other supported\nexchanges;</li>\n<li>validate resources against applicable profiles and terminology;</li>\n<li>retrieve, create, update, or persist resources where supported;</li>\n<li>execute declared FHIR operations;</li>\n<li>apply applicable business and access-control rules; and</li>\n<li>return FHIR resources, Bundles, operation results, or <code>OperationOutcome</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Conformance expectations</h3>\n<p>A Responder <strong>SHALL</strong>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>process supported requests according to applicable Nigeria Core requirements;</li>\n<li>enforce applicable cardinalities, invariants, terminology bindings, required\nreferences, and <strong>Must Support</strong> expectations;</li>\n<li>use governed identifiers and terminology where specified;</li>\n<li>publish or make available an accurate <code>CapabilityStatement</code>;</li>\n<li>advertise only capabilities it can reliably support;</li>\n<li>return FHIR-conformant responses; and</li>\n<li>return an appropriate <code>OperationOutcome</code> when a request cannot be processed.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The Responder <strong>SHOULD</strong> provide sufficient error information for correction\nwithout exposing sensitive implementation details.</p>\n<p>Access to technically available information <strong>SHALL</strong> remain subject to\napplicable authentication, authorisation, privacy, consent, and security rules.</p>\n<h3>Capability discovery</h3>\n<p>The Responder's <code>CapabilityStatement</code> <strong>SHOULD</strong> identify supported FHIR\nversion, profiles, resources, interactions, operations, search parameters,\nformats, security requirements, and relevant limitations.</p>\n<h3>Relationships</h3>\n<p>The Responder commonly interacts with the <strong>Nigeria Core Requestor, Registry\nService, Terminology Service,</strong> and <strong>Conformance and Sandbox Service</strong>.</p>\n<p>A system may act as both Requestor and Responder.</p>\n</div></td></tr></table></div>"
  ] ;
